From: EvilPatrick06 <187923600+EvilPatrick06@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:16:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): the screen watcher polls each home under its
 own terminal policy

The serve backend's watcher re-reads every served home's Bot Screen when its
runtime files move, and stops idle screens, under HERMES_HOME alone. The
status read re-attaches a sandbox-hosted screen (_owned_sandbox_env), so it
acquires a terminal environment, and with only the home bound it did so on
the LAUNCH profile's terminal policy. Every serve process watching a home
whose screen came up built a new container keyed and mounted as that
profile but rooted at its own launch profile's terminal.cwd.

Measured on a six-profile host: one profile's screen came up, and within
0.4 s five docker containers keyed as that profile (each mounting another
profile's work folder at /workspace) and one local environment were built,
one per serve process watching the home.

The poll now binds the watched home's full runtime scope (home, secrets,
terminal), the composition @_profile_scoped binds for a display.* call and
methods_profiles._hermes_home_scope binds for config reads (#120726). The
launch home keeps its frozen launch env. No external secret sources are
hydrated: the bodies read runtime files and status only.
